---
import LegalPageLayout from '../components/legal/LegalPageLayout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '../lib/sanity/data';
---

<LegalPageLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  eyebrow="COMMERCIAL TERMS OF BUSINESS"
  subheading="Master commercial framework governing service agreements, certified custody transfer, secure sanitisation warranties, and environmental compliance for Techsteps UK Limited."
  metaTitle="Terms & Conditions | Commercial Framework | Techsteps UK"
  metaDescription="Techsteps UK Terms & Conditions. Governing commercial contracts, chain of custody, data sanitisation warranties, environmental liabilities, and service delivery."
  complianceBadge="Governed by Laws of England & Wales"
  activeSlug="terms-and-conditions"
  lastUpdated="February 2026"
>
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      1. Scope &amp; Application of Terms
    </h2>
    <p>
      These Standard Terms and Conditions of Business ("Terms") apply to all commercial proposals, service orders, contracts, and operational execution provided by {siteSettings.legalName} ("Techsteps", "Contractor", "we", "us", or "our") to corporate clients, public authorities, and commercial organizations ("Client", "you").
    </p>
    <p>
      Our services encompass four specialised operational divisions:
    </p>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-600">
      <li><strong>Information Management:</strong> Physical document archiving, heritage storage, media vaulting, digital mailrooms, and digitisation scanning.</li>
      <li><strong>IT Lifecycle Services &amp; Destruction:</strong> Certified ITAD, remarketing, component recovery, secure hardware testing, and zero-landfill e-waste recycling.</li>
      <li><strong>Secure Shredding &amp; Document Integrity:</strong> On-site mobile shredding, off-site high-torque shredding, DIN 66399 cross-cut particle destruction, and uniform destruction.</li>
      <li><strong>Moving &amp; Relocation Services:</strong> Data centre server de-racking, laboratory moves, sequential archival relocations, and specialist business moves.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      2. Quotations, Bookings &amp; Contract Formation
    </h2>
    <p>
      All written quotations provided by Techsteps remain valid for thirty (30) calendar days from the date of issue unless explicitly stated otherwise. A legally binding contract comes into existence upon the earliest of: (a) Client issuing a written purchase order, (b) Client digitally accepting a service proposal, or (c) Techsteps dispatching logistics vehicles pursuant to Client instructions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any modifications, special service level agreements (SLAs), or deviations from these Standard Terms must be agreed in writing and signed by an authorized Director of Techsteps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      3. Chain of Custody &amp; Asset Handover
    </h2>
    <p>
      Legal and physical chain of custody transfers to Techsteps at the exact point when a joint Asset Handover Manifest or Waste Transfer Note is countersigned by our BS 7858 security-screened operative and the Client’s authorized site representative.
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600">
      <li>
        <strong>Security-Screened Personnel:</strong> Techsteps warrants that all operatives involved in collections, transit, and facility operations have completed comprehensive five-year employment history vetting and criminal record screening conforming to BS 7858.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Dedicated Secured Transport:</strong> Transit occurs in solid-sided, deadlocked vehicles fitted with active GPS telematics, remote engine immobilization, and dual-monitored panic systems.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Custodial Integrity:</strong> Handover manifests establish unambiguous inventory counts. Client is responsible for ensuring that all assets slated for release are authorized, unencumbered by third-party liens, and free of hazardous biological or radioactive contamination.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      4. Data Sanitisation &amp; Destruction Warranties
    </h2>
    <p>
      Techsteps warrants that all digital media, data-bearing devices, and confidential physical archives accepted for sanitisation or destruction will be processed strictly in accordance with client-specified service levels:
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">A. ADISA 8.0 &amp; NIST 800-88 Rev 1 Software Overwriting</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Cryptographic erasure and multi-pass magnetic overwriting verifying 100% sector sanitisation with cryptographically signed tamper-proof audit trails for each individual device serial number.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">B. Physical Destruction to DIN 66399 Security Levels</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Mechanical shredding, degaussing, and disintegration achieving particle standards from Level P-4 to P-7 (paper) and Level H-5 to H-7 (hard drives/SSDs).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">C. Certificate of Destruction (CoD)</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">
          A legally binding Certificate of Destruction and Asset Reconciliation Report will be issued within five (5) working days following completed processing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      5. Environmental Compliance (WEEE &amp; Duty of Care)
    </h2>
    <p>
      Techsteps operates under full waste carrier licensing granted by the Environment Agency. We legally warrant that:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
      <li>Zero unprocessed electronic waste will be illegally exported outside the UK or European economic frameworks.</li>
      <li>Zero electronic or confidential fractions will be routed directly to UK municipal landfill facilities.</li>
      <li>All end-of-life materials undergo certified secondary raw material refining through accredited UK smelting partners.</li>
      <li>Duty of Care Waste Transfer Notes are issued and catalogued for statutory inspection periods.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      6. Invoicing, Payment Terms &amp; Value Recovery
    </h2>
    <p>
      Standard commercial payment terms are thirty (30) calendar days from invoice date for approved corporate account holders, unless alternative credit terms are agreed in writing. Value recovery rebates (yielded from enterprise ITAD hardware remarketing) will be credited against collection invoices or remitted to the Client’s nominated corporate account within 30 days of inventory liquidation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      7. Limitation of Liability &amp; Insurance
    </h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in these Terms limits or excludes liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or any matter where it is unlawful under English law to exclude liability.
    </p>
    <p>
      Techsteps maintains comprehensive commercial insurances:
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono space-y-1">
      <div>&bull; <strong>Employer's Liability:</strong> £10,000,000</div>
      <div>&bull; <strong>Public &amp; Products Liability:</strong> £10,000,000</div>
      <div>&bull; <strong>Professional Indemnity / Cyber Liability:</strong> £5,000,000</div>
      <div>&bull; <strong>Goods in Transit Insurance:</strong> £250,000 per vehicle consignment</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      8. Governing Law &amp; Jurisdiction
    </h2>
    <p>
      These Terms and Conditions, and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with their subject matter or formation (including non-contractual disputes), shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales. The parties irrevocably agree that the courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction.
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono">
      <div><strong>Legal Inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:legal@techsteps.co.uk" class="text-emerald-700 hover:underline">legal@techsteps.co.uk</a></div>
      <div><strong>Contract Management:</strong> {siteSettings.phone}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalPageLayout>
